Package: decklock
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: DeckLock packaging <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/yan-vidal/DeckLock
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
# Comment lines are stripped when this is emitted: a binary DEBIAN/control has
# no comment syntax. Shared libraries, libgtk4-layer-shell0 included, come from
# dpkg-shlibdeps.
# The GStreamer plugins are loaded through dlopen, so nothing in the binary
# reveals them and they are declared by hand, as in the other recipes.
Depends: @DEPENDS@, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-libav, libpam-modules
Recommends: gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, systemd
X-Payload-Sha256: @SHA256@
Description: Customizable Wayland lock screen with GTK4 settings and bundled media
 DeckLock locks a Wayland session through ext-session-lock-v1, with a native
 GTK4 settings application, configurable themes, procedural and video media,
 an on-screen keyboard and offline bilingual help.
 .
 Real locking requires a compositor that implements ext-session-lock-v1. KDE
 Plasma and GNOME do not, and X11 is not supported.
 .
 This package is built against the Ubuntu 26.04 library stack. It does not run
 on Debian 13, which packages gtk4-layer-shell 1.0.4, below the 1.2 floor that
 dpkg-shlibdeps derives from this binary's symbol versions.
